  "key_finding": "On the smaller box Omega1 the certified Dirichlet LG lower bounds lie strictly ABOVE the true ground energy (true lambda1(R3) <= -0.5509673): N=48 gives lambda1^D(Omega1) >= -0.5508692, N=64 gives >= -0.5508177. The Dirichlet eigenvalue provably OVERESTIMATES lambda1(R3), and the certified truncation-error lower bound RISES with N (>= 9.8e-5 at N=48, >= 1.50e-4 at N=64) as the discretization sharpens -- a rigorous proof of the limitation of Dirichlet truncation on a small box. Doubling to Omega2 removes the bias: the true value sits inside the N=64 Dirichlet bracket [-0.5514408, -0.5509673], truncation error < 4.8e-4 and not sign-definite."
